{"name":"Barrett Quince","hex":"#f5d1b2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quince","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pear-shaped fruit of a small tree of the rose family, Cydonia oblonga.","The deciduous tree bearing such fruit, native to Asia."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of quinceañera."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quince"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quince","blocks":[{"text":"The quince is the sole member of the genus Cydonia in the Malinae subtribe of the Rosaceae family. It is a deciduous tree that bears hard, aromatic bright golden-yellow pome fruit, similar in appearance to a pear. Ripe quince fruits are hard, tart, and astringent. They are eaten raw or processed into jam, quince cheese, or alcoholic drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pancrace_Bessa00.jpg/330px-Pancrace_Bessa00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quince","wikidata":"Q43300"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_quince_flower_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Cydonia.jpg/250px-Cydonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/